    "narrative": "The engine for Ghost Ride the WHIP today is undeniably **Corbin Carroll**, whose 87.14 efficiency score leads the roster as he faces Sugano in a park environment that adds a massive +14% boost to his output. While **James Wood** (68.90) and **Mickey Moniak** (68.66) offer high-floor production, **Corbin Carroll** remains our primary catalyst for stolen base upside; his pairing with a favorable matchup against Sugano maximizes both his speed and power profiles. **Josh Naylor** also warrants attention with a strong 73.91 score, as the model heavily favors his matchup against Buehler (+19% SP skill advantage), ensuring he occupies a critical core spot in our 1B slot today.\n\nThe most difficult bench decision centered on **Austin Riley**, who finished with a 51.43 score. Despite his pedigree, **Austin Riley** was edged out by the superior environmental efficiency of **Kyle Karros** (61.47), whose favorable park factors and the +15% SP skill boost from the Rodriguez matchup provided just enough marginal gain to clinch the 3B start. We are closely monitoring the 34% rain risk surrounding **Vinnie Pasquantino**; while his 65.10 score is robust thanks to a strong platoon advantage, the volatility of the weather coupled with the \u201cLineup Pending\u201d status for players like **Gabriel Moreno** and **Dalton Rushing** necessitates constant vigilance before first pitch. If any of these projected spots shift, we will pivot to the high-efficiency potential sitting on the bench to ensure our category coverage remains consistent with our stolen base mandate.",
